The AP6275P firmware on the BCM43752 (18.35.387.23.146, which is
built for the bcmdhd driver) does not acknowledge the mailbox
BRCMF_H2D_HOST_D3_INFORM handshake. brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3() then
times out waiting for the D2H D3 ack and aborts the suspend/freeze
callback with -EIO, which breaks both S3 suspend and hibernation.

The device is powered off by the PM layer regardless once the
callback returns success, and brcmf_pcie_pm_leave_D3() already takes
care of the resume side by falling back to a proper brcmf_pcie_probe()
re-init when the hardware did not preserve state. So, treat a missing
D3 ack as best-effort: log a message and continue instead of failing.
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -2591,9 +2591,7 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_pm_enter_D3(struct device *dev)
 	wait_event_timeout(devinfo->mbdata_resp_wait, devinfo->mbdata_completed,
 			   BRCMF_PCIE_MBDATA_TIMEOUT);
 	if (!devinfo->mbdata_completed) {
-		brcmf_err(bus, "Timeout on response for entering D3 substate\n");
-		brcmf_bus_change_state(bus, BRCMF_BUS_UP);
-		return -EIO;
+		brcmf_info("No D3 ack from firmware, continuing with suspend\n");
 	}
 
 	devinfo->state = BRCMFMAC_PCIE_STATE_DOWN;
